      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Published by Oxford University Press and JSCR Publishing Ltd. All rights reserved. © The Author 2016.",
        "AbstractText": "Adverse reaction to metal debris (ARMD) in total hip arthroplasty surgery is a well-known problem. We present the case of a unipolar hemiarthroplasty requiring revision within 18 months of insertion secondary to an adverse reaction to metal debris. This case demonstrates a rare cause for failure of a hemiarthroplasty following a fragility fracture. We feel that ARMD should be considered in all cases where pain and dysfunction in the presence of any hip prosthesis cannot be explained by routine investigations."
      },
